# Gumroad upload guide - {{ title }}

Open **Products > New product**. Gumroad does not offer a product-creation API, so creation is manual.

## 1. Basics
- Product type: **Digital product**
- Name: `{{ copy.short_title }}`
- Price: **${{ "%.2f"|format(price) }}** (Gumroad charges a flat 10% fee; 30% on sales through Gumroad Discover - fees can change, check their pricing page).

## 2. Cover & thumbnail
- Cover: `{{ cover }}` (1280 x 720 px, 16:9)
- Thumbnail: `{{ thumb }}` (600 x 600 px). Gumroad crops the thumbnail from the centre, so keep key content centred.

## 3. Description
```
{{ description }}
```

## 4. Content
Upload:
{% for f in files -%}
- `{{ f }}`
{% endfor %}
## 5. Settings
- Add 3-5 tags/categories relevant to: {{ copy.tags[:5]|join(', ') }}
- Turn on a short **discount code** for your first customers (e.g. 25% off for two weeks).
- Enable **"Let customers pay what they want"** only if you want a minimum-price test.
- Write a short **receipt message** thanking the buyer and linking to your shop/Pinterest.

## 6. Publish checklist
- [ ] Download your own product after publishing to test the delivery
- [ ] Check the product page on mobile
- [ ] Link the Gumroad page from your Pinterest pins and bio
